Contrast: The contrast refers to the degree of visual distinction that is evident between associated
colors. f - Faint: Evident only on close examination.
d - Distinct: Readily seen but contrast only moderately with the color to which they are
compared. p - Prominent: Contrast strongly with the color to which they are compared.
Shape: The shape of some mottles is significant and is often described by common words like streaks,
bands, tongues, tubes, and spots.
Concentration Within The Soil
Nodules and concentrations are discrete bodies strong enough and distinct enough to be removed from
the soil intact. Nodules are formed by the filling of cicada larva channels and are distinguished from
concretions on the basis of internal organization.
Amount or quantity: The amount or quantity of concentrations refers to the relative volume of a horizon
or other specified unit occupied by the bodies.
Size: The size may be measured directly or given by the classes listed below. The following size classes
are used: f - Fine: Smaller than 2 mm. m - Medium: 2 to 5 mm.
